From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:20:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] api: no phone-home from the web UI (OpenX6X00)

The web UI asked two things of the internet each time it was opened,
and the radio asked on its behalf:

- /api/new-release-check asked api.getpat.io for the latest release. It
  answers 204 (no newer release) now: this Pat comes with the radio's
  updates.
- GET /api/winlink-account/password-recovery-email sent the callsign and
  the password to winlink.org. It answers a placeholder address now,
  which the UI takes for "an address is set". Setting an address (PUT)
  still goes to winlink.org.

The version report and the periodic recovery-email check of the app
itself stay off through version_reporting_disabled in the config.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
